# StudyLens Coding Standards (OpenCode Rules)

These rules are binding for all contributions to this repository.

## Architecture
- Use a modular, feature-oriented structure. Keep domain logic out of UI components and route handlers.
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind. Manifest V3 only.
- Backend: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async) + Pydantic v2.
- No direct DOM mutation from React components; content scripts live in `content/` and background logic in `background/`.

## TypeScript
- `strict: true`, `noImplicitAny: true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true`.
- ZERO `any` types. Use `unknown` + narrowing, generics, and explicit API contracts.
- All API responses must have explicit TypeScript interfaces matching backend Pydantic schemas.
- Use `const` by default, `let` only when reassignment is required.

## Python / FastAPI
- All request/response models must use Pydantic v2 `BaseModel` with field validators.
- Use `python-jose`/PyJWT for tokens, passlib bcrypt for hashing.
- No bare `except:`. Catch specific exceptions and return clean API errors.
- Use async SQLAlchemy sessions via dependency injection.
- Type hints on all functions. Run `ruff` + `mypy`.

## Security
- No secrets in code. Use `.env` + Pydantic Settings.
- Strict CORS: only extension origin(s) and local dev. No `*` in production.
- MV3 CSP: no remote code, no eval, no inline scripts.
- Sanitize all extracted page text before sending to backend/Ollama.
- Store tokens only in `chrome.storage` (never localStorage).

## Error Handling
- Extension: graceful degradation when backend/Ollama is down — show health indicator, never crash.
- Backend: global exception handler returns structured `{detail, error_code}` JSON.
- Log errors server-side with request IDs.

## Testing & Quality
- Frontend: Vitest + React Testing Library.
- Backend: pytest + httpx AsyncClient.
- Lint before commit: eslint, prettier, ruff, mypy.
